              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When it comes to maintaining your fleet, even small decisions can make a big impact, especially when it comes to the parts keeping your trucks on the road. If you’re weighing the pros and cons of OEM versus aftermarket components, you’re not alone. Fleet managers across Florida often ask the same question: Which parts offer the best value, performance, and peace of mind? Here’s a clear breakdown of what you need to know when choosing between OEM and aftermarket fleet freight truck parts.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-difference",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding the Difference",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "difference"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-difference-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Before we dive into recommendations, let’s quickly clarify what sets OEM and aftermarket parts apart:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-difference-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "stack2",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) parts",
                        "points": [],
                        "rule": "ink",
                        "label": "OEM",
                        "url": "/parts",
                        "intro": "Designed and built by the same manufacturer that produced your vehicle. These parts are made to fit your truck precisely, down to every bolt and seal."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Aftermarket parts",
                        "points": [],
                        "rule": "accent",
                        "label": "AFTERMARKET",
                        "url": "/aftermarket",
                        "intro": "Produced by independent manufacturers. While many are high quality, they’re typically designed to work across a range of truck makes and models rather than a single brand."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 20
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-difference-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Both options have their place, but understanding how each affects your operations is the key to making the right investment.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-oem",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Choose OEM?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-oem"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-why-oem-1",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "stack2",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Precision Fit and Compatibility",
                        "points": [],
                        "label": "OEM · 01",
                        "intro": "<a href=\"/parts\">OEM parts</a> are engineered for your specific truck model, which means you can count on a perfect fit. This reduces the risk of issues during installation or operation—no need to second-guess whether it will work."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Reliable Performance",
                        "points": [],
                        "label": "OEM · 02",
                        "intro": "Because these parts are made to the exact standards of your truck’s original design, you can expect consistent and dependable results. When you’re managing time-sensitive routes or heavy-duty jobs, that kind of reliability matters."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Manufacturer Support and Warranty",
                        "points": [],
                        "label": "OEM · 03",
                        "intro": "<a href=\"/parts\">OEM parts</a> often come with a manufacturer-backed warranty. If your truck is still under coverage, OEM components can ensure you’re still compliant with your warranty’s terms. That extra peace of mind can save you thousands over the life of the vehicle."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Resale and Long-Term Value",
                        "points": [],
                        "label": "OEM · 04",
                        "intro": "Sticking with <a href=\"/parts\">OEM parts</a> can boost the resale value of your truck and reduce long-term maintenance costs. It’s an investment that often pays off through lower risk and greater efficiency."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 20
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-when-oem",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When OEM Makes the Most Sense",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "when-oem"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-oem-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<a href=\"/parts\">OEM fleet freight truck parts</a> are generally the best choice when you’re dealing with critical systems like the engine, transmission, or brakes—components where precision, compatibility, and reliability are non-negotiable. They’re also the better option if your vehicle is still under the original manufacturer’s warranty, as using <a href=\"/parts\">OEM parts</a> helps preserve that coverage. If you operate a standardized fleet, <a href=\"/parts\">OEM parts</a> also help ensure consistency and streamline maintenance across vehicles, taking the guesswork out of repairs and replacements.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-aftermarket",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Case for Aftermarket Parts",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "aftermarket"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-aftermarket-1",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "stack2",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Lower Initial Costs",
                        "points": [],
                        "label": "AFTERMARKET · 01",
                        "intro": "<a href=\"/aftermarket\">Aftermarket parts</a> are generally more budget-friendly, especially for routine repairs or replacing parts on older vehicles. If you’re maintaining a large fleet, those savings can stack up quickly."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Greater Selection and Availability",
                        "points": [],
                        "label": "AFTERMARKET · 02",
                        "intro": "Because multiple companies manufacture aftermarket components, you often have more choices. That means you can find the part you need more easily—and sometimes faster—than with OEM-only options."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Comparable Performance from Trusted Brands",
                        "points": [],
                        "label": "AFTERMARKET · 03",
                        "intro": "There are several aftermarket manufacturers that produce parts equal in quality to OEM. In some cases, you might even find components that offer improvements or longer service intervals."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Ideal for Out-of-Warranty Vehicles",
                        "points": [],
                        "label": "AFTERMARKET · 04",
                        "intro": "For trucks no longer covered by manufacturer warranties, aftermarket parts provide a practical solution, especially for non-critical components like lights, mirrors, or hoses."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 20
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-when-aftermarket",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When Aftermarket Is the Right Call",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "when-aftermarket"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-aftermarket-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<a href=\"/aftermarket\">Aftermarket parts</a> can be a smart solution in many scenarios. If you’re maintaining older or out-of-warranty trucks, <a href=\"/aftermarket\">high-quality aftermarket options</a> can provide comparable performance to OEM parts at a lower cost. These parts are also a practical choice for non-essential or cosmetic replacements, like lights or mirrors, where functionality matters more than brand alignment. For businesses watching the bottom line or managing a high volume of repairs, aftermarket parts can offer the flexibility and value needed to stay efficient, particularly when sourced from trusted vendors with a proven track record.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-recommend",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What We Recommend at Sun State International",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "recommend"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-recommend-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "We know no two fleets are exactly alike, which is why we offer both OEM and <a href=\"/aftermarket\">high-quality aftermarket fleet freight truck parts</a>. Our team is here to help you make the right decision based on your truck’s make, current condition, warranty status, and operational needs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "pull-recommend-2-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginTop": 28,
                      "marginBottom": 28
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "pull-recommend-2",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderTopWidth": 1,
                          "borderBottomWidth": 1,
                          "borderLeftWidth": 0,
                          "borderRightWidth": 0,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 24,
                          "paddingBottom": 24
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "pull-recommend-2-text",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "You won’t get a one-size-fits-all answer here—just honest advice, reliable inventory, and support you can count on.",
                            "align": "left",
                            "width": "full"
                          },
                          "styles": {
                            "base": {
                              "fontSize": 17,
                              "fontWeight": "800",
                              "lineHeight": 1.8,
                              "textColor": "ink"
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-recommend-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "We also back every installation with the expertise of our certified technicians. Our service bays are equipped to handle everything from <a href=\"/service\">preventive maintenance</a> to full-scale repairs. Whether you’re replacing one part or outfitting an entire fleet, we’re ready to help you get it done right.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "links-recommend-4",
                  "type": "link-cards",
                  "props": {
